From a3ad6bb17b49f01beb23b63be3ac5ac08c897880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:35:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DSi Wi-Fi chip: wlan0 net device, connect to an open network,
 data path

Step 5 of docs/ATHEROS-PLAN.md:
- wlan0 (registered at boot, down): "ifconfig wlan0 up" uploads the
  firmware, connects the HTC services, waits for WMI ready, scans, and
  keeps the chip up with the antenna on it; "ifconfig wlan0 down"
  disconnects and gives the antenna back. Refused while nds is up.
- A kernel thread does every ARM7 request: queued Ethernet frames go out
  as mailbox data packets on endpoint 2 (word 0x2008; dst, src, length,
  LLC/SNAP, EtherType, data); every 20 ms it fetches up to 8 packets (WMI
  events, data -> netif_rx_ni).
- "echo connect [name] > /proc/dsiwifi2" joins an open network from the
  scan (the strongest without a name) with dswifi's sequence (BSS filter,
  scan/channel params, synchronize, power mode, pstream, WSC, disconnect
  timeout, keepalive, connect); carrier on the connect event, off on
  disconnect; "echo disconnect".
- WMI events the driver does not know are logged (12 at most).
- ARM7: a receive with 0 ms looks once.
- wifi-dsi-test: wlan0 up, connect, DHCP, ifconfig, ping 8.8.8.8 and
  google.com, all in /tmp/wlan0-test.log (in the card log).
- The firmware part tables are static: gcc 4.0.4 crashed (unrecognizable
  insn) compiling upload() with them on the stack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
